y seized power  the acting leader of suchi's democratic  party who remains in hiding  promised a revolution to end the  february coup during his first public  address given from a secret location  he appealed for people to join the  uprising to restore democracy  the pope made another appeal for peace  in syria during his traditional sunday  blessing from saint peter's square  francis offered prayers for the country  on the 10th anniversary  of its civil war it is the 21st  century's deadliest conflict  the pontiff called for a new commitment  from the international community  to end the violence and urged all sides  involved in the fighting to show signs  of good  to give the exhausted population a  glimmer of hope  chile is now one of the top countries in  the world when it comes to its covet 19  vaccination program more than 25 percent  of the population  has received at least one shot the  country of 19 million people  is currently the vaccine champion of  latin america the situation is far  better than at the start of the pandemic  when the chilean government was  criticized for its inability to trace  and isolate  infected people up next a dying woman's  final wish and how she had to say  goodbye to her family  covet 19 has affected just about every  part of our lives  and it can have a profound effect on  death because of pandemic restrictions  a palliative care home in quebec was  forced to wheel a patient  out into the cold the reason so she  could see her loved ones  one last time mike armstrong has the  heart-wrenching moment  her family wants you to see  it was clear what this was a final  goodbye justin boucha the woman on that  bed  had one last wish to see her family  together the kovit 19 rules at the  palliative care center in alma quebec  don't allow more than 10 visitors  bouchard has more than 10  brothers and sisters add to that her two  children  and six grandchildren  my son says having to choose who in the  family could see her and who couldn